  "trace":{"definition":"apply(Base12<>, Patches</a:0->Q,/l:1->R>)","source":"Design record: versions world, depth pass (11-04). Illustrative local model."},
  "walkthrough":{
    "scope":"Design exercise, not a completed kernel run. Proposed finite contract: versions documents with 12 paths, 2 revisions and 2 patch steps. The judge checks the whole document and charged layer-0 calls; the learner sees only the declared read interface.",
    "inventions":[
      {"kind":"object","declaration":"obj Revision = Quot[Pair<Doc, Int>, canon_revision] L1","check":"Validate the typed pair and a terminating canonicalizer; reject malformed documents.","call":"Construct Revision<Doc<12>, 2> and unfold its canonicalizer to given calls.","verify":"Exhaustively check canonicalization idempotence, validity and interface equivalence for every member of the finite contract.","promote":"Store the object with its exact domain, hash and interface contract; only then show construction as one boundary step."},
      {"kind":"operation","declaration":"op apply_guarded(r: Revision, p: Patch) -> Revision = apply_if_old_values_match(r, p) L2","check":"Resolve Revision, Patch and the given guard and update operations; check result sort.","call":"On a stale second guard, unfold to Bottom(guard), with no committed changes.","verify":"Exhaustively compare both Ok and Bottom with an independent guarded-update table over the finite contract, including full state and cost.","promote":"Store the operation with the checked guard and cost contract; outside the scope, unfold or refuse the short step."},
      {"kind":"combinator","declaration":"comb @apply_chain[step](r: Revision, ps: List<Patch>) -> Revision = @bounded_rec[step](r, ps) L3","check":"Check the plugged step's type, decreasing remaining-patch count and finite fuel.","call":"Unfold both patch steps; a stale second guard leaves the whole chain uncommitted.","verify":"Bounded check for every listed step operation and patch sequence of length at most 2, comparing unfoldings including failures and costs.","promote":"Keep the operation-family and length bound with the promoted combinator; never widen to arbitrary steps."},
      {"kind":"observation","declaration":"obs ?revision{r: Revision} -> Int = read_revision(r) L2","check":"Check it reads only a granted layer-0 revision probe on Revision, not the sealed document or a combinator.","call":"Read the revision from an existing Revision value without changing the state; a prior successful chain could produce such a value but is not a dependency of this observation.","verify":"Exhaustively check permission safety, noninterference, determinism and equality to the full-state judge projection on the finite contract.","promote":"Store the declared visible channel and scope; the hidden document stays available only to the judge."}
    ]
  },
